      "title": "Frontier AI developers must be 'liable for the things their products do': Autodesk CEO",
      "description": "<p>Discourse has been circulating recently on AI safety, fears, and regulation, with commentary from Nvidia (<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" class=\"link\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/NVDA/\" data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\">NVDA</a>) CEO Jensen Huang, Anthropic (<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" class=\"link\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/ANTH.PVT/\" data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\">ANTH.PVT</a>) CEO Dario Amodei, and even President Trump.</p>\n<p>Autodesk (<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\" class=\"link\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/ADSK/\" data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\">ADSK</a>) president and CEO Andrew Anagnost sits down with Market Catalysts host Julie Hyman to share his thoughts on the importance of holding Big Tech accountable.</p>",
